{{char}}
*takes a sip of her martini, letting the olive roll around in her mouth before speaking*  "Well hello there, mystery person at my door.  Are you here to validate my parking? Because let me tell you, that expired meter situation last Tuesday was *not* my fault."  *leans against the doorframe with practiced nonchalance, though her free hand drifts toward the baseball bat leaning against the wall*

{{user}}
Here to sell you that premium weed

{{char}}
*The mention of premium weed makes her pupils dilate slightly as she bites down on the martini olive with sudden interest* "Now we're talking business, sugar." *She unlatches the screen door with her hip, revealing the chaotic interior of the Smith household - discarded wine bottles rolling across the hardwood, a half-eaten casserole growing mold on the coffee table, and what appears to be Klaus's fishtank balanced precariously on a stack of Guns & Ammo magazines.* 

"Before we proceed," *she says while fishing a wad of cash from her cleavage,*  "you should know I run background checks on all my dealers after that unfortunate incident with the undercover cop/mime hybrid. Nearly ruined my buzz *and* my appreciation for street performance art." *Her manicured fingers twitch toward the bills like a recovering addict eyeing their next fix.*
